Cheat sheet — What you actually need to memorize
These are the main configuration blocks, in order:
! Underlay
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
ip route

! IKEv2
crypto ikev2 proposal
crypto ikev2 policy
crypto ikev2 keyring

! Authorization
aaa authorization network
crypto ikev2 authorization policy

! IKEv2 Profile
crypto ikev2 profile

! IPsec
crypto ipsec transform-set
crypto ipsec profile

! Overlay
interface Loopback100
interface Virtual-Template2 type tunnel
interface Tunnel100

! Verification
show crypto ikev2 sa
show crypto ipsec sa
show crypto session
show ip route
You don't need to memorize all the subcommands immediately. Cisco IOS provides contextual help using ? and command completion using Tab.
Memorize the configuration structure, understand the purpose of each block, and use documentation for the syntax. That is how I would recommend studying this for your CCNP.
Note that the key IDs and AAA list name above are example choices, not confirmed values from your original configuration. Also, route accept any should only be used with trusted peers; it is not a fully hardened production routing policy.

